{"name":"Filthy Brown","hex":"#e8aa08","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"filthy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with filth; very dirty.","Obscene or offensive."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make very dirty; to saturate something with dirt.","To cover in filth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/filthy"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Filthy (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Filthy\" is a song recorded by American singer Justin Timberlake for his fifth studio album, Man of the Woods (2018). RCA Records released the song for digital download and streaming on January 5, 2018, as the album's lead single. Timberlake co-wrote and co-produced the track with Timbaland and Danja, with James Fauntleroy and Larrance Dopson providing additional songwriting. It was also recorded at Conway Recording Studios, based in Hollywood, Los Angeles. The song is an electro-funk, electropop, and R&B tune in the key of G major that comprises funky electro-R&B elements and features tongue-in-cheek lyrics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Justin_Timberlake_-_Filthy_%28Official_Single_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filthy_(song)"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_